Package: stablr
Title: Kinetic Modeling of Pharmaceutical Stability Data
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Federico", family = "Ferrari", email = "federico.ferrari@msd.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "Samantha", family = "Gleich", email = "samantha.gleich@msd.com", role = c("aut")),
    person(given = "Michael", family = "Johnson", email = "michael.johnson6@msd.com", role = c("aut")),
    person(given = "Qiaohui", family = "Zhou", email = "qiaohui.zhou@msd.com", role = c("aut")),
    person("Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA and its affiliates", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
    )
Description: Fits kinetic models to pharmaceutical stability data using
    nonlinear least squares. Supported models include the Sestak-Berggren
    degradation model (Sestak and Berggren (1971)
    <doi:10.1016/0040-6031(71)85051-7>; Perez-Maqueda et al. (2006)
    <doi:10.1021/jp064792g>) solved as an ordinary differential equation,
    single-step degradation, and parallel degradation into two products.
    Temperature and relative humidity dependence of reaction rates is
    described with the Arrhenius and humidity-modified Arrhenius equations
    (Waterman et al. (2007) <doi:10.1007/s11095-006-9201-4>). Provides
    confidence, prediction and tolerance intervals for model predictions,
    with tolerance intervals following Krishnamoorthy and Mathew (2009)
    <doi:10.1002/9780470473900>, predictions under time-varying temperature
    profiles, and simulation of stability data.
